––– comment –––
Starts of the watchdog and crash dumps of every node; node 1 was killed with SIGKILL (the watchdog stops too and logs no 'killed dirtily') and started again; the others started once; no crash dump anywhere
––– input –––
for n in 1 2 3; do L=/var/log/manticore-$n/searchd.log; echo "node $n starts=$(grep -c 'watchdog: main process .* forked ok' $L) killed=$(grep -c 'killed dirtily' $L) dumps=$(grep -c 'CRASH DUMP' $L)"; done
